{
  "id": "halden-border-human-red",
  "title": "Halden border — Red played by a person",
  "description": "Halden border for two sides: Blue runs civil dispatch and the defence of Objective KNUT while a second player commands Red, whose recce and four tanks start on the border road, with more crossing at 15 and 23:30 minutes. Red gets a new call every few minutes (scout, probe, take the Tistedal heights, attack KNUT) and decides which to follow and when to strike; it sees Blue only through its own recces and tanks, as Blue sees Red only through its observation post and recces. Blue's calls follow the same timeline as the scripted exercise. A fictional exercise around Halden with no national markings: calls, forces and numbers are authored for play, not claims about real services or armed forces. How to play: Blue picks \"Blue (one person)\" or splits \"Civil desks\" and \"Blue military\", and Red picks \"Red commander\" on another iPad; the role chip reopens the groups dialog. Tap a call to see its suggested units, then tap Dispatch. Tap one of your units to highlight it, then tap a call, a place or an identified enemy to send it there. + on a unit's row adds the next target you tap to the end of its chain, so Red can route its tanks through waypoints before the attack.",
  "objectives": [
    "Blue: dispatch every call, all closed by 30:00, and reach C-17 Bakke, the 22:30 top-priority call, within six minutes.",
    "Blue: hold Objective KNUT, so Red never completes an Attack call.",
    "Red: take Objective KNUT, a tank completing an Attack call.",
    "Red: lose fewer steps than Blue."
  ],
